## 3. Environment Setup (Reproducible)

### 3.1 Hardware Requirements

- **CPU**: ≥ 8 cores (for federated client simulation)
- **RAM**: ≥ 16 GB
- **GPU**: ≥ 8 GB (optional, for faster training; the paper reports on neuromorphic hardware but simulation runs on CPU/GPU)
- **Disk**: ~5 GB (datasets + artifacts)
- **Neuromorphic simulation**: `hardware/neuromorphic_simulator.py` emulates Intel Loihi 2 and BrainChip Akida timing/energy profiles using calibrated tables from published datasheets (0.1 pJ/spike for Loihi 2, 0.78 ms/query for Akida).

### 3.2 Quick Start

```bash
# 1. Clone
git clone https://github.com/<your-org>/NQAL-DoH.git
cd NQAL-DoH

# 2. Create environment (Python 3.10+)
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate         # Linux/macOS
# .venv\Scripts\activate.bat      # Windows

# 3. Install
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Verify environment
python -c "from hardware.neuromorphic_simulator import NeuromorphicSimulator; print('OK')"

# 5. Generate datasets
python data/generate_dataset.py --config config/default.yaml --seed 42

# 6. Train NQAL (federated + adversarial)
python train.py --config config/default.yaml

# 7. Evaluate (reproduces Table 2 + metrics)
python evaluate.py --config config/default.yaml

# 8. Full reproduction (all tables/figures, ~45 min on 8-core CPU)
bash run_all_experiments.sh
